              "One of China's top economic aides Liu He is in the U.S. this week to discuss trade cooperation between China and the United States. He is the director of China's Office of the Central Leading Group for Financial and Economic Affairs. Liu will ascertain what the Trump administration is looking for from China, as trade relations between the two countries become increasingly strained. It seems unlikely, however, that Liu will be successful in making great strides with U.S",
              "Liu is meeting with U.S. Trade Representative Robert Lighthizer, Treasury Secretary Steven Mnuchin and economic advisor Gary Cohn to talk about bilateral trade and economic relations. Chinese State Councilor Yang Jiechi met with U.S. Secretary of State Rex Tillerson last month to discuss similar issues. The visit resulted in the announcement that both countries would resume talks under the Comprehensive Economic Dialogue, which ended in an impasse last year.",
              "The situation has already worsened even with Liu in negotiations. Just as Liu began his trip in the United States, the U.S. Commerce Department decided that aluminum foil from China was benefiting unfairly from government subsidies. The U.S. will impose anti-dumping duties on China as a result. Chinese officials were unhappy with this action, stating that the unilateral retaliatory measure contradicts WTO rules. By contrast, just this week, China has removed import duties on U.S",
